stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> BLEScan
    BLEScan --> WifiSelection: robot discovered
    BLEScan --> Failed: permission denied / timeout
    WifiSelection --> BLEScan: cancel Wi-Fi selection / refocus search
    WifiSelection --> EncryptedBluFi: SSID + transient password ready
    EncryptedBluFi --> Failed: STA_CONN_FAIL / GATT error / timeout
    EncryptedBluFi --> BackendConfirmation: STA_CONN_SUCCESS
    EncryptedBluFi --> BackendConfirmation: owned reconnect timeout + fresh post-handoff heartbeat
    BackendConfirmation --> Rename: first-pair claim confirmed
    BackendConfirmation --> Success: offline robot registered and online
    BackendConfirmation --> DeviceHome: owned robot reconnects online
    BackendConfirmation --> Failed: bounded claim/online timeout
    Failed --> BLEScan: double-click BOOT and retry Bluetooth
    Failed --> WifiSelection: correct Wi-Fi password
    Failed --> [*]: give up
    Rename --> Success: provisioning complete
    Success --> [*]
    DeviceHome --> [*]

    note right of EncryptedBluFi
      SSID/password travel only over encrypted BluFi.
      A successful GATT write is not provisioning success.
    end note

    note right of BackendConfirmation
      Backend owns claim, ownership, token, status, and heartbeat.
      A reconnect timeout is recoverable only when online=true and
      lastSeenAt is valid and not older than the current handoff.
      Stale or missing heartbeat timestamps remain failures.
      ESP server is contacted only after firmware is online.
    end note

    note right of BLEScan
      Every focused search owns a unique run id.
      Blur, cancel, or a newer focus invalidates stale async work.
    end note
